      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Thus, the diameter of the sphere is $6$ inches, and the radius $r$ is $3$ inches (half the length of the cube edge).\n\nThe volume $V$ of a sphere is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3. \\]\n\nSubstituting the radius of the sphere into the formula, we get:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3)^3. \\]\n\nNow calculate $(3)^3$:\n\\[ 3^3 = 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 27. \\]\n\nSo,\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (27). \\]\n\nPerform the multiplication within the parentheses:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3}(27)\\pi. \\]\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n\\[ V = 36\\pi. \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the inscribed sphere is $\\boxed{36\\pi}$ cubic inches.",
