      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the volume of the inscribed sphere, we need to find the radius of the sphere. Since the sphere is circumscribed around the cube and the cube's edges correspond to the diameter of the sphere, the radius of the sphere is half of the cube's edge length.\n\n1. The edge length of the cube is given as 6 inches.\n2. As the cube is inscribed in the sphere, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube.\n3. Therefore, the diameter of the sphere is 6 inches.\n4. The radius of the sphere is half of the diameter, which is \\( \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\) inches.\n5. Now, to find the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere, we use the formula \\( V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3 \\).\n6. Substituting \\( r = 3 \\):\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3 \\]\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (27) \\]\n\\[ V = \\frac{4 \\times 27 \\pi}{3} \\]\n\\[ V = \\frac{108 \\pi}{3} \\]\n\\[ V = 36 \\pi \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the inscribed sphere is \\(\\boxed{36\\pi}\\) cubic inches.",
